From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: nss: create the mesh dbg_infra directory once

ath11k_nss_init() calls ath11k_debugfs_nss_soc_create() for every radio
and again after every firmware restart, and each call creates
dbg_infra directly under the module's ath11k debugfs directory. Every
call after the first logs

  debugfs: Directory 'dbg_infra' with parent 'ath11k' already present!

and creates nothing. Its two files, links and mpp_mode, work on
module-wide state (the mesh_vaps list and the mpp_mode variable), so the
directory is only needed once for the module's lifetime. Return early
when it already exists.

Seen on IPQ5018 + QCN6122: the warning at the second radio's NSS init
and at every in-place recovery.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/debug_nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/debug_nss.c
@@ -910,6 +910,15 @@
 {
 	struct dentry *debugfs_dbg_infra;
 
+	/* Its files are module-wide (mesh_vaps, mpp_mode), but this runs for
+	 * every radio and again after every firmware restart.
+	 */
+	debugfs_dbg_infra = debugfs_lookup("dbg_infra", debugfs_ath11k);
+	if (debugfs_dbg_infra) {
+		dput(debugfs_dbg_infra);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	debugfs_dbg_infra = debugfs_create_dir("dbg_infra", debugfs_ath11k);
 
 	debugfs_create_file("links", 0200,
